https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z26BvHOD_sg  (Capo 0) (MC1)

TIP:  It’s important to get the strumming pattern down to emulate Iz’s ukulele.  For the intro it’s a downstroke at the beginning of each chord change and then 8th notes, so D DUDUDU.  For the verse it’s either this same pattern or a backed off D DUD DU.  

TIP:  It’s subtle, but the second (Am) chord in the intro is an (Am7) so hold form and add your pinky to note <g> on the 1st string/3rd fret.  Try not to hit the 4th string.  If you want to keep it simple, just play another (Am).

TIP:  To play the (D7sus4) from the (Dm7) just hold form and add your pinky to the 1st string/3rd fret.  When moving to the (G) you can then hold the pinky where it is.  To simplify this bit, just play another (F) and hold through to the (F).  


